    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch07-05: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.62";
    dc:description "Many published observations make cross-population tests possible, but the key fear and persecution variables require substantial compilation. Causal acquisition speed remains difficult to isolate.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Relate flight-initiation distance or approach tolerance across populations to quantified duration and intensity of human persecution, controlling for body size, urbanization, and phylogeny. Increasing fear with exposure supports the claim.";
